An elevated twist on classic pumpkin pie from Epicurious. Pure pumpkin purée is spiced with cinnamon, ginger, nutmeg, and cloves, then blended with a rich, from-scratch deep amber caramel cream before baking in a crisp blind-baked crust.

*Adapted from [Epicurious](https://www.epicurious.com/recipes/food/views/caramel-pumpkin-pie-236428).*

## Ingredients

### Crust
- 1 standard round pie dough (homemade or store-bought)
- Pie weights or dried beans (for blind baking)

### Caramel Custard Filling
- 1 cup granulated sugar
- ⅓ cup water
- 2 cups heavy cream, divided
- 1 can (15 oz) solid-pack pure pumpkin purée (not pumpkin pie mix)
- 1 ¼ teaspoons ground ginger
- 1 ¼ teaspoons ground cinnamon
- ¼ teaspoon freshly grated nutmeg
- Pinch of ground cloves
- Scant ½ teaspoon salt
- 4 large eggs, lightly beaten

### Serving
- Lightly sweetened freshly whipped cream

## Instructions

1. **Shape and Chill the Pastry Shell:** Set your oven rack in the middle position and preheat to 375°F (190°C). Roll out your pie pastry on a floured surface to a 14-inch circle. Ease it without stretching into a 10-inch metal quiche pan featuring a removable bottom (or a 9- to 10-inch deep pie plate). Trim dough evenly along the fluted rim. Refrigerate for 30 minutes to chill and prevent shrinkage.
2. **Blind-Bake to a Crisp Finish:** Dock the base of the cold shell several times with the tines of a fork. Fit a piece of aluminum foil over the dough, filling it generously with dried beans or ceramic pie weights. Place on a baking sheet and bake for 18 to 20 minutes until the edges appear set. Lift away foil and weights, then return to the oven for 10 minutes longer until the bottom crust is dry, crisp, and lightly golden. Transfer to a rack and let cool completely.
3. **Make the Homemade Amber Caramel Cream:** Place the sugar and water into a deep heavy saucepan over medium-high heat. Swirl gently until the crystals dissolve, then bring to a rapid boil. Allow the syrup to bubble untouched (swirling the pot every so often) for roughly 10 minutes until it develops a rich amber-copper hue. Immediately drop heat to low and cautiously pour in 1 cup of heavy cream (expect it to foam up vigorously). Stir with a wooden spoon until smooth and molten, then blend in the second cup of heavy cream. Bring just to a gentle simmer, then take off the burner.
4. **Mix the Spiced Pumpkin Custard:** In a spacious mixing bowl, combine the pumpkin purée with ginger, cinnamon, grated nutmeg, ground cloves, and salt. While whisking steadily, slowly pour the warm caramel cream into the spiced pumpkin. Add the beaten eggs, whisking until the custard is glossy, fluid, and uniform.
5. **Bake to a Gentle Set:** Pour the custard filling right into the cooled crust. Bake at 375°F (190°C) for 55 to 60 minutes. The filling is properly cooked when it rises around the outer ring and the center has a very soft wobble when tapped.
6. **Cool, Unmold, and Serve:** Let the pie rest on a cooling rack for at least 2 hours at room temperature; this resting time allows the egg-and-caramel custard to set cleanly for neat slices. Gently push the base up to release the fluted rim, slice into wedges, and serve with clouds of fresh whipped cream.

## Notes

- **Caramel Tip:** Watch the sugar closely in the final minutes—it transitions quickly from golden amber to burnt. As soon as it reaches deep amber, reduce heat and add the cream immediately.
- **Deep Dish:** Using a 10-inch fluted tart or quiche pan with a removable bottom yields clean, beautiful fluted slices.
